    {
      "v": 2,
      "zh": "每 逢 七 日 的 第 一 日 ， 各 人 要 照 自 己 的 進 項 抽 出 來 留 著 ， 免 得 我 來 的 時 候 現 湊 。",
      "en": "On the first day of the week, each of you should set aside some income[NOTE:1] and save[NOTE:2] it to the extent that God has blessed you,[NOTE:3] so that a collection will not have to be made[NOTE:4] when I come.",
      "notes": [
        "Grk “set aside, storing whatever he has been blessed with.”",
        "Grk “set aside, storing.” The participle θησαυρίζων (thēsaurizōn) indicates the purpose or result of setting aside the extra income.",
        "“To the extent that God has blessed you” translates an awkward expression, “whatever has been prospered [to you].” This verb has been translated as an active with “God” as subject, taking it as a divine passive.",
        "Grk “so that collections will not be taking place.”"
      ],
